Sigh. Tourists have credit cards, which can be used to unlock chests
without messing around with forcing or what-have-you. Takes about 1/10
the time, and makes much less noise.

As a side note, who thinks tourists are the most fantastic characters
ever? I love tourists, because:

1) They start with lots of food, so they won't starve before reaching
the nutrient-rich lower levels of the dungeon.

2) The ever-useful credit card and infinite-charges expensive camera
are fantastic.

3) Who else starts with a nifty, impressive-looking Hawaiian shirt?
NOBODY!

4) Tourists usually have a pretty good distribution of abilities.
Constituition and Charisma are usually high; intelligence and strength
are good, dex and wisdom occasionally cause problems.

5) If they find a shop early in the game, they can instantly become kick-ass
characters, because most start with about 800 gp!

Well, I've raved enough for now.

